  "title": "The Watermachine: multifunctional area for flood protection and improved water quality - Kristalbad, Enschede",
  "summary": "Kristalbad, a 40-hectare Dutch area, utilizes the Water-machine concept for flood protection, water purification, enhancing ecological connectivity and creating a recreational zone. It stores 187000 m 3 of water to mitigate flood risks in nearby cities during heavy rainfall and purified water aids agriculture during dry spells. Kristalbad is an area of about 40 hectares located in the east of the Netherlands between the cities of Enschede (160.000 inhabitants) and Hengelo (81.000 inhabitants). This is one of the last remaining green areas between these two cities, playing a role for ecosystem-based adaptation to cope with potential climate change related impacts.",
